   "stem": {
      "text": "Find the value of \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{x^{4} - 4x + 3}{x^{3} - 3x + 2} \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": 2
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "As \\( x \\to 1 \\), the numerator \\( x^{4} - 4x + 3 \\) tends to \\( 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "As \\( x \\to 1 \\), the denominator \\( x^{3} - 3x + 2 \\) tends to \\( 0 \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The numerator and the denominator both tend to 0, so the form is \\( \\frac{0}{0} \\) and L'Hospital's rule applies. Differentiate the numerator and the denominator separately: the limit equals \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{4x^{3} - 4}{3x^{2} - 3} \\).",
         "mathjson": 0
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "The new numerator and denominator both tend to 0 again, so the form is still \\( \\frac{0}{0} \\) and the rule applies once more. Differentiate each separately again: the limit equals \\( \\lim_{x \\to 1} \\frac{12x^{2}}{6x} \\).",
         "mathjson": 12
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "At \\( x = 1 \\) this numerator is \\( 12 \\) and this denominator is \\( 6 \\), which is not 0, so the limit is \\( 2 \\).",
         "mathjson": 2
      }
   ],
